<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Declaration of the Independence of New Zealand</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1835">1835</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as He Whakaputanga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Declaration of the Independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, in Māori He Whakaputanga o te Rangatiratanga o Nu Tireni, was signed at Waitangi on 28 October 1835 by 34 northern Māori chiefs, organised by the British Resident <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-busby">James Busby</a>. It declared New Zealand an independent state under the United Tribes, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> held by the hereditary chiefs, and asked King William IV to act as protector. By 1839 it had 52 signatories; it preceded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-waitangi">Treaty of Waitangi</a> of 1840.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/declaration-of-the-independence-of-new-zealand.jpg" alt="Declaration of the Independence of New Zealand" width="320" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archives New Zealand from New Zealand · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:He_Whakaputanga_o_te_Rangatiratanga_o_Nu_Tireni_(known_as_The_Declaration_of_Independence)_(Page_1_of_3),_1835_(10430000633).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
